meta {
  name: Supertrend Filter
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/filter/supertrend?timeframes=M5,M15,M30&direction=UP
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  timeframes: M5,M15,M30
  direction: UP
  ~tickers: TQQQ,SQQQ
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  # Supertrend Filter
  
  Screens a universe of tickers by Supertrend DIRECTION across one or more
  timeframes. Read-only — no orders, no state change.
  
  A ticker PASSES only if its Supertrend matches `direction` on EVERY requested
  timeframe (AND). Uses the app's Supertrend params (webull.supertrend, 7/3) on
  the latest COMPLETED bar.
  
  ## Query
  - `timeframes` — comma-separated ST timeframes (e.g. M5,M15,M30). Supported:
    M1, M5, M15, M30, M60, M120, M240, D, W, M, Y. Default M15.
  - `direction`  — UP or DOWN. Default UP.
  - `tickers`    — optional comma-separated symbols to screen instead of the
    universe.txt file (e.g. TQQQ,SQQQ). Omit to screen the universe file.
  
  ## Response (200)
  A plain JSON array of the tickers that matched `direction` on ALL requested
  timeframes, e.g. [ "TQQQ", "SQQQ" ].
  
  ## Errors
  - `400` — invalid direction/timeframe, or nothing to screen.
}
